  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to discharge the burden of proof, on the balance of probability, to demonstrate that the rear outbuilding at 9 Charter Square has been in continuous use as a separate, clearly subdivided and self-contained dwelling (a separate planning unit) for a minimum period of four years. The evidence submitted is addressed to the main property and does not sufficiently distinguish the occupation of the outbuilding as a separate unit from the main dwelling. Therefore, the requirements of Section 171B(2) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 have not been met, and the change of use to a separate dwellinghouse is not immune from enforcement action."
  ],
